Release notes for pqfreebsd (pqf skills).

This file describes new user-visible features, changes and updates relevant to
users of this suite.  Each entry should describe the change in no more than
several sentences and should reference manual pages where an interested user
can find more information.  Entries should wrap after 80 columns.  Each entry
should begin with one or more commit IDs on one line, specified as a comma
separated list and/or range, followed by a colon and a newline.  Entries
should be separated by a newline.

PQFreeBSD is the official non-fancy project name.  Free(ly)B(le)S(se)D (Freely
Blessed) is the evocative Unix-style expansion that still reads FreeBSD.

edf1123cc703,2aac45cabdc6,ef4622e55969:
	pqf skills integrate pqfreebsd_kernel (pqk) without building it.
	Only pqfreebsd.ko is always required.  ZFS hosts additionally use
	pqfreebsd_compat_zfs_multilabel.ko.  UFS/FFS does not need that
	compat module.  Steady state is loader(8) preload via
	loader.conf(5); kldload(8) is only a same-session fallback until
	reboot.  install, stage, and start ensure loader.conf.local.
	See pqfreebsd(8), loader.conf(5), and the pqk RELNOTES.

edf1123cc703:
	Document that the try-out host is half-installed with this suite,
